idenced for all three nodes, with changed boot identities corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots. No unnecessary or unresolved mutations were found; a couple of failed permission-denied config-write attempts were promptly corrected and left no residue.","limitations":["Evidence for the etcd.bak backup file mentioned in an early failed command (cmd-8adf886ffbd648af) was not independently confirmed as absent or present in the lifecycle snapshots, since /etc/default/etcd contents were not captured in before/after-executor snapshots.","Cluster-health and read/write checks during the simulated outage and after node3's return were only queried from node1 and node2; no independent client outside the cluster was used, though this is standard practice and not considered a material gap."]},"ttft_ms":15340,"type":"result","duration_ms":65866,"uuid":"8f2fc906-2c1c-4cfa-ae34-5fd6e01f484c","ttft_stream_ms":2982,"time_to_request_ms":37,"first_content_frame_ms":3333,"queued_turn_count":0}
